Create `src/types.ts` with TypeScript interfaces for Ralph's core data structures. Port these from the shapes used in the shell/Python code.

**RalphConfig** — matches ralph.json shape:
```ts
interface RalphConfig {
  projectName: string;
  projectDescription: string;
  healthCheck: string;
  defaultTestCommand: string;
  implementationFile: string;
  truncateText: boolean;
  summarize: { claudeMdPattern: string };
  narration: {
    enabled: boolean;
    voice: string;
    ntfyTopic: string;
  };
}
```

**Task** — matches tasks.json task shape (see `lib/tasks.schema.json` for the authoritative schema):
```ts
interface Task {
  id: number;
  priority: number;
  title: string;
  description?: string;
  directory?: string;
  status: 'pending' | 'in-progress' | 'complete' | 'blocked';
  files?: string[];
  tests?: string[];
  completedAt?: string;
  completedBy?: string;
  notes?: string;
  dependencies?: number[];
  model?: 'opus' | 'sonnet';
  agent?: string;
}
```

**AgentInfo** — matches the shape from `_ralph_discover_agents()` in `lib/ralph_config.sh`:
```ts
interface AgentInfo {
  name: string;
  description: string;
  model: string;
  file: string;
}
```

Export all interfaces. Also export type guard functions (`isValidConfig`, `isValidTask`) that validate unknown data against the expected shapes. These should check required fields exist and have correct types.

Write tests in `test/types.test.ts` that verify the type guards accept valid data and reject malformed data (missing fields, wrong types).

Create src/test-validator.ts and test/test-validator.test.ts. Port the post-iteration test validation from ralph_execute.sh (lines 551-627).

Implement:
- validateTaskTests(opts: { task: Task, tasksFilePath: string, projectRoot: string }): Promise<{ status: 'passed' | 'failed' | 'error' | 'skipped', message?: string }>

Behavior:
- Read task meta to get test commands from task.tests array
- If no tests defined, return { status: 'skipped' }
- Check if the task was marked complete in tasks.json (re-read file to get current status)
- Run each test command from the task's resolved directory (projectRoot + task.directory) with a 120s timeout
- Smart failure detection: distinguish 'can't run' (missing script, MODULE_NOT_FOUND, command not found → exit code 127) from 'ran but failed' (non-zero exit with test output)
- On real test failure: revert task status to 'in-progress' in tasks.json, append failure note to task.notes, return { status: 'failed', message }
- On infrastructure error (can't run): append note but DON'T revert status, return { status: 'error', message }
- On all tests passing: return { status: 'passed' }

Make the file I/O (reading/writing tasks.json) injectable or use the filesystem directly as the shell version does.

TDD. Create and export a function `parseReviewFeedback(content: string)` in src/commands/plan.ts. It parses the review-feedback.md format and returns structured data:

```ts
interface ReviewDimension {
  name: string;
  score: 'PASS' | 'WARN' | 'FAIL';
  issues: string[];
}
interface ReviewResult {
  dimensions: ReviewDimension[];
  verdict: 'PASS' | 'NEEDS_WORK';
  summary: string;
}
```

The input format has sections like:
```
Coverage: PASS | WARN | FAIL
- [issue text]

## Verdict: PASS | NEEDS_WORK
[summary text]
```

Handle edge cases: missing dimensions, malformed input (return NEEDS_WORK verdict as safe default). Write tests first in test/commands/plan.test.ts covering: all-pass case, mixed scores, NEEDS_WORK verdict, malformed input, missing sections.

TDD. Add `spawnPostTaskReviewer()` to `src/post-task-reviewer.ts`, following the `spawnReviewer()` pattern in `src/commands/plan.ts` (lines 622-663).

Interface:
```ts
interface SpawnPostTaskReviewerOpts {
  projectRoot: string;
  dataDir: string;
  task: { id: number; title: string; description: string; files?: string[]; tests?: string[]; directory?: string };
  diff: string;
  log: string;
  files: string[];
  streamOpts?: ProcessStreamOptions;
  deps?: { spawn?: typeof spawn; processStreamFn?: typeof processStream };
}
```

Implementation:
- Build system prompt via `buildPostTaskReviewPrompt()`
- Build user prompt via `buildPostTaskReviewUserPrompt()`
- Spawn `claude` with args: `-p`, `--append-system-prompt <systemPrompt>`, `--allowedTools Read,Glob,Grep,Edit,Write`, `--output-format stream-json`, `--model sonnet`, `--verbose`
- Unset ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in env (same pattern as spawnReviewer)
- Pipe user prompt to stdin, close stdin
- Pipe stdout through processStream (use deps.processStreamFn or default)
- Wait for close event, return `{ exitCode }`

Tests mock spawn to verify: correct claude args, stdin receives user prompt, processStream called on stdout, exit code returned.

TDD. Add `runPostTaskReview()` to `src/post-task-reviewer.ts`.

Interface:
```ts
interface RunPostTaskReviewOpts {
  projectRoot: string;
  dataDir: string;
  task: Task;
  taskStatus: string;
  beforeSha: string | null;
  config: RalphConfig;
  streamOpts?: ProcessStreamOptions;
  deps?: {
    captureGitSha?: typeof captureGitSha;
    getGitDiff?: typeof getGitDiff;
    spawnPostTaskReviewer?: typeof spawnPostTaskReviewer;
    log?: (...args: any[]) => void;
  };
}
```

Skip conditions (return early, log reason):
1. `config.review?.postTask` is not true
2. `taskStatus` is not 'complete'
3. `beforeSha` is null
4. Current SHA equals beforeSha (no commits made) — call `deps.captureGitSha(projectRoot)`

Happy path: call `deps.getGitDiff(projectRoot, beforeSha)`, then `deps.spawnPostTaskReviewer()` with task + diff data. Log start/completion. Return void (informational, never throws).

Wrap the entire function body in try/catch — log errors but never throw (review must not break the run loop).

Tests cover: each skip condition returns early without spawning, happy path calls getGitDiff and spawnPostTaskReviewer with correct args, errors are caught and logged.

Bug: `startNarrationServer()` in `src/narration.ts` waits 1s then does a single health check. Kokoro TTS takes 3-5s to init, so the check fires too early and throws.

Fix (TDD — write tests first):

1. In `test/narration.test.ts`, add tests for:
   - Retry succeeds on Nth attempt (mock `checkNarrationHealth` to return false N-1 times then true)
   - Early exit on first success (verify health check is not called more than necessary)
   - Throws after all retries exhausted (mock health check to always return false)

2. In `src/narration.ts` `startNarrationServer()`, replace:
   ```ts
   await new Promise<void>((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 1000));
   const healthy = await checkNarrationHealth(socketPath);
   if (!healthy) {
     throw new Error('Narration server failed health check after startup');
   }
   ```
   With a retry loop: poll `checkNarrationHealth()` up to 10 times with 1s intervals (~10s max wait). Return PID on first successful PONG. Throw only if all 10 retries are exhausted.

3. Run `bun test test/narration.test.ts` to confirm all tests pass.

